# Omni-fetch — Local & Modular RAG Upgrade Plan

## Overview
This plan upgrades the Omni-fetch RAG architecture into a fully modular, extensible, and **100% free/local-first runnable system**. Based on your requirements and `OmniFred_Upgrade_Plan.md`, we are replacing all cloud-dependent dependencies (**NeMo Guardrails**, **Portkey Gateway**, and **Qdrant Cloud**) with robust, zero-cost, open-source local equivalents:

| Cloud Component | Replaced With (100% Free / Local / Open-Source) |
|---|---|
| **NeMo Guardrails / Cloud Guardrails** | **Local Guardrails Engine** (`app/guardrails/local_guard.py`): Pure local regex + semantic embedding + lightweight ONNX/Rule-based jailbreak, PII masking, and schema validation. Zero external cloud API calls required. |
| **Portkey AI Gateway** | **Local LLM Resilience Gateway** (`app/gateway/local_gateway.py`): Local multi-model router with automatic fallback (Local Ollama / Local HuggingFace / Gemini free tier / mock local fallback), retry exponential backoff, rate limiter, and local SQLite audit ledger. |
| **Qdrant Cloud** | **Local Vector Store Ecosystem** (`app/services/retrieval/vectorstore/`): Embedded Local Qdrant (`path="./data/qdrant_db"`), Local ChromaDB (`PersistentClient`), and In-Memory/Disk FAISS (`faiss-cpu`). |

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Default Local-First Configuration**:
> - Embeddings default to `local` (`sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` or `all-mpnet-base-v2` downloaded and cached locally).
> - Vector DB defaults to `chroma` / `qdrant-embedded` (storing vectors directly to local disk in `./data/`).
> - LLM Gateway defaults to local Ollama / local fallback / Gemini API key if present.
> - All packages used will be freely pip-installable (`chromadb`, `faiss-cpu`, `qdrant-client`, `sentence-transformers`, `flashrank`, `langgraph`, `pydantic`).

